      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 2179057469866936249, guid: 41d89b59fe3e9964a83686ff24b7d0c5, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'One of the earliest examples of robotics in entertainment is the self-playing
        piano.

        As early as the late 1800s, player pianos used mechanical
        systems and punched paper rolls to press keys automatically following stored
        instructions (an early form of programming).

        Today, modern self-playing
        pianos like the Disklavier and Spirio use digital music data, sensors, and
        precise motor control.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
